In solving word problems involving permutation, we can use the following formulas: 
\begin{align} P &= \frac{n!}{(n - r)!} \text{ for the linear form taken r at a time} \\ P &= \frac{n!}{a!b!c!...} \text{ for distinguishable} \\ P &= (n-1)! \text{ for circular} \\ P &= \frac{(n-1)!}{2} \text{ for circular withour lock} \\ P &= \frac{n!}{2} \text{ for circular with lock} \end{align}
